  "text": "In distillation processes, bulk inference applies labels to data. In this form of distillation, a larger llm acts as the teacher model role and a smaller llm acts as the student model role. The teacher model labels a dataset. A team could run a large toxicity scoring model offline to label training data, which creates labeled data that can sometimes contain more information than the teacher model itself was trained on. Alternatively, the teacher model could use the labeled data to distill a student model small enough to score live comments. Through labels, the teacher model passes knowledge to the distilled llm and gives numerical scores to the student model. A richer training signal enables the distilled llm to predict borderline cases, predict clearly positive cases, and predict clearly negative cases.",
